    summary: "Observational data suggest GLP-1 receptor agonists reduce obesity-related cancer incidence, but confounding is severe. Propose an RCT, or prospective cancer adjudication embedded in ongoing cardiovascular outcome trials, with incident obesity-related cancer as the primary endpoint in adults aged 50-70 with BMI of 30 or more.",
    hypothesis: "GLP-1 receptor agonist therapy reduces incidence of obesity-related cancers by at least 20% over seven years.",
