    hypothesis: "Programme-wide opportunistic salpingectomy reduces high-grade serous ovarian cancer incidence by at least 40% in the exposed cohort at 15 years.",
    rationale: "Tubal origin of high-grade serous cancer; no known effect on ovarian function; salpingectomy is also a more effective sterilisation than ligation.",
